React queues state updates until the event handler finishes. A state setter does not change the value in the current render.

When the next value depends on the previous one, pass an updater function to `setCount`. TypeScript infers the parameter type from the state type. See the [React reference](https://react.dev/reference/react/useState).

```tsx
const [count, setCount] = useState<number>(0);
setCount(previous => previous + 1);
```
